IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc22-nunavut.l4 -- sections 573 to 573.2 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part XIX.1, Nunavut Court of Justice). Part agent ccc22. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE (the text's own words bring the case within the rule); JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Tags in the comments: [M-a] a failed "if"/"where" or a flat negative counted as the text's no; [M-b] a prohibition or grant limited by its own wording counted as NOT the text's no (NOTHING);
-- [F:...] a fork line for NOTES.md (may-if, may-where, entitled, duty, unless). Section 2 terms and other parts' answers are INPUTS named for their section.

§ `Section 573 -- Nunavut Court of Justice`

-- The holders of the powers, duties and functions that (1) lets a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice exercise or perform.
-- src:12465 | 573 (1) The powers to be exercised and the duties and functions to be performed under this Act by a court of criminal jurisdiction, a summary conviction court, a judge, a provincial court judge, a justice or a justice of the peace may be exercised or performed by a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice.
@ref s 573(1) (src:12465-12465)
DECLARE `s 573(1) the holder the Act gives the power, duty or function to` IS ONE OF
    `s 573(1) a court of criminal jurisdiction`
    `s 573(1) a summary conviction court`
    `s 573(1) a judge`
    `s 573(1) a provincial court judge`
    `s 573(1) a justice`
    `s 573(1) a justice of the peace`
    `s 573(1) some other holder`

-- src:12465 | 573 (1) The powers to be exercised and the duties and functions to be performed under this Act by a court of criminal jurisdiction, a summary conviction court, a judge, a provincial court judge, a justice or a justice of the peace may be exercised or performed by a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice.
@ref s 573(1) (src:12465-12465)
GIVEN `the person acting is a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      holder IS A `s 573(1) the holder the Act gives the power, duty or function to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573(1) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may exercise the power or perform the duty or function` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person acting is a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be exercised or performed by a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice"
        IF holder EQUALS `s 573(1) some other holder` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "by a court of criminal jurisdiction, a summary conviction court, a judge, a provincial court judge, a justice or a justice of the peace"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12467 | (2) A power exercised or a duty or function performed by a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice under subsection (1) is exercised or performed by that judge as a judge of a superior court.
@ref s 573(2) (src:12467-12467)
GIVEN `the power was exercised or the duty or function performed by a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573(2) the power, duty or function is exercised or performed as a judge of a superior court` MEANS
    IF `the power was exercised or the duty or function performed by a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "exercised or a duty or function performed by a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice under subsection (1)"

-- (3): the bar: subsection (2) does not authorize a judge presiding at a preliminary inquiry to grant a remedy under section 24 of the Charter. JUST TRUE where the bar applies.
-- src:12469 | (3) Subsection (2) does not authorize a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice who is presiding at a preliminary inquiry to grant a remedy under section 24 of the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms.
@ref s 573(3) (src:12469-12469)
GIVEN `the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice is presiding at a preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the remedy is a remedy under section 24 of the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573(3) subsection (2) does not authorize the judge to grant the remedy` MEANS
    IF `the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice is presiding at a preliminary inquiry` AND `the remedy is a remedy under section 24 of the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not authorize a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice who is presiding at a preliminary inquiry to grant a remedy under section 24"

§ `Section 573.1 -- Application for review -- Nunavut`

-- src:12471 | 573.1 (1) An application for review may be made by the Attorney General or the accused, or by any person directly affected by the decision or order, to a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut in respect of a decision or order of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice
-- src:12472 | (a) relating to a warrant or summons;
-- src:12473 | (b) relating to the conduct of a preliminary inquiry, including an order under subsection 548(1);
-- src:12474 | (c) relating to a subpoena;
-- src:12475 | (d) relating to the publication or broadcasting of information or access to the court room for all or part of the proceedings;
-- src:12476 | (e) to refuse to quash an information or indictment; or
-- src:12477 | (f) relating to the detention, disposal or forfeiture of any thing seized under a warrant or order.
@ref s 573.1(1) (src:12471-12477)
DECLARE `s 573.1(1) who applies` IS ONE OF
    `s 573.1(1) the Attorney General`
    `s 573.1(1) the accused`
    `s 573.1(1) a person directly affected by the decision or order`
    `s 573.1(1) someone else`

-- src:12471 | 573.1 (1) An application for review may be made by the Attorney General or the accused, or by any person directly affected by the decision or order, to a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut in respect of a decision or order of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice
-- src:12472 | (a) relating to a warrant or summons;
-- src:12473 | (b) relating to the conduct of a preliminary inquiry, including an order under subsection 548(1);
-- src:12474 | (c) relating to a subpoena;
-- src:12475 | (d) relating to the publication or broadcasting of information or access to the court room for all or part of the proceedings;
-- src:12476 | (e) to refuse to quash an information or indictment; or
-- src:12477 | (f) relating to the detention, disposal or forfeiture of any thing seized under a warrant or order.
@ref s 573.1(1) (src:12471-12477)
DECLARE `s 573.1(1) the kind of decision or order` IS ONE OF
    `s 573.1(1)(a) relating to a warrant or summons`
    `s 573.1(1)(b) relating to the conduct of a preliminary inquiry, including an order under subsection 548(1)`
    `s 573.1(1)(c) relating to a subpoena`
    `s 573.1(1)(d) relating to the publication or broadcasting of information or access to the court room`
    `s 573.1(1)(e) to refuse to quash an information or indictment`
    `s 573.1(1)(f) relating to the detention, disposal or forfeiture of any thing seized under a warrant or order`
    `s 573.1(1) some other kind of decision or order`

-- src:12471 | 573.1 (1) An application for review may be made by the Attorney General or the accused, or by any person directly affected by the decision or order, to a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut in respect of a decision or order of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice
-- src:12472 | (a) relating to a warrant or summons;
-- src:12473 | (b) relating to the conduct of a preliminary inquiry, including an order under subsection 548(1);
-- src:12474 | (c) relating to a subpoena;
-- src:12475 | (d) relating to the publication or broadcasting of information or access to the court room for all or part of the proceedings;
-- src:12476 | (e) to refuse to quash an information or indictment; or
-- src:12477 | (f) relating to the detention, disposal or forfeiture of any thing seized under a warrant or order.
@ref s 573.1(1) (src:12471-12477)
GIVEN applicant IS A `s 573.1(1) who applies`
      `the application is made to a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision or order is one of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `s 573.1(1) the kind of decision or order`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573.1(1) an application for review may be made` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF applicant EQUALS `s 573.1(1) someone else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "by the Attorney General or the accused, or by any person directly affected by the decision or order"
        IF NOT `the application is made to a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut"
        IF NOT `the decision or order is one of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of a decision or order of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice"
        IF kind EQUALS `s 573.1(1) some other kind of decision or order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "(a) relating to a warrant or summons; (b) ... (f) relating to the detention, disposal or forfeiture of any thing seized under a warrant or order"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2): the bar. JUST TRUE where the section bars review.
-- src:12478 | Limitation
-- src:12479 | (2) A decision or order may not be reviewed under this section if
-- src:12480 | (a) the decision or order is of a kind that could only be made in a province or a territory other than Nunavut by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552; or
-- src:12481 | (b) another statutory right of review is available.
@ref s 573.1(2) (src:12478-12481)
GIVEN `the decision or order is of a kind that could only be made in a province or a territory other than Nunavut by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another statutory right of review is available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573.1(2) the section bars review of the decision or order` MEANS
    IF `the decision or order is of a kind that could only be made in a province or a territory other than Nunavut by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552` OR `another statutory right of review is available`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A decision or order may not be reviewed under this section if" (neither (a) nor (b) holds: the bar does not apply) [M-a]

-- src:12471 | 573.1 (1) An application for review may be made by the Attorney General or the accused, or by any person directly affected by the decision or order, to a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut in respect of a decision or order of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice
-- src:12472 | (a) relating to a warrant or summons;
-- src:12473 | (b) relating to the conduct of a preliminary inquiry, including an order under subsection 548(1);
-- src:12474 | (c) relating to a subpoena;
-- src:12475 | (d) relating to the publication or broadcasting of information or access to the court room for all or part of the proceedings;
-- src:12476 | (e) to refuse to quash an information or indictment; or
-- src:12477 | (f) relating to the detention, disposal or forfeiture of any thing seized under a warrant or order.
-- src:12478 | Limitation
-- src:12479 | (2) A decision or order may not be reviewed under this section if
-- src:12480 | (a) the decision or order is of a kind that could only be made in a province or a territory other than Nunavut by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552; or
-- src:12481 | (b) another statutory right of review is available.
@ref s 573.1(1) and (2) (src:12471-12481)
GIVEN `the answer of s 573.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 573.1(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573.1 an application for review may be made, subject to subsection (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer of s 573.1(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A decision or order may not be reviewed under this section if"
        OTHERWISE `the answer of s 573.1(1)`

-- (3): the grounds. "only if the judge is satisfied that" closes the gate, so no ground (or no satisfaction) is JUST FALSE.
-- src:12482 | Grounds of review
-- src:12483 | (3) The judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may grant relief under subsection (4) only if the judge is satisfied that
-- src:12484 | (a) in the case of any decision or order mentioned in subsection (1),
-- src:12485 | (i) the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice failed to observe a principle of natural justice or failed or refused to exercise the judge’s jurisdiction, or
-- src:12486 | (ii) the decision or order was made as a result of an irrelevant consideration or for an improper purpose;
-- src:12487 | (b) in the case of a decision or order mentioned in paragraph (1)(a), that
-- src:12488 | (i) the judge failed to comply with a statutory requirement for the making of the decision or order,
-- src:12489 | (ii) the decision or order was made in the absence of any evidence that a statutory requirement for the making of the decision or order was met,
-- src:12490 | (iii) the decision or order was made as a result of reckless disregard for the truth, fraud, intentional misrepresentation of material facts or intentional omission to state material facts,
-- src:12491 | (iv) the warrant is so vague or lacking in particularity that it authorizes an unreasonable search, or
-- src:12492 | (v) the warrant lacks a material term or condition that is required by law;
-- src:12493 | (c) in the case of a decision or order mentioned in paragraph (1)(b), that the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice
-- src:12494 | (i) failed to follow a mandatory provision of this Act relating to the conduct of a preliminary inquiry,
-- src:12495 | (ii) ordered the accused to stand trial when there was no evidence adduced on which a properly instructed jury acting reasonably could convict, or
-- src:12496 | (iii) discharged the accused when there was some evidence adduced on which a properly instructed jury acting reasonably could convict;
-- src:12497 | (d) in the case of a decision or order mentioned in paragraph (1)(c) or (d), that the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice erred in law;
-- src:12498 | (e) in the case of a decision or order mentioned in paragraph (1)(e), that
-- src:12499 | (i) the information or indictment failed to give the accused notice of the charge,
-- src:12500 | (ii) the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice did not have jurisdiction to try the offence, or
-- src:12501 | (iii) the provision creating the offence alleged to have been committed by the accused is unconstitutional; or
-- src:12502 | (f) in the case of a decision or order mentioned in paragraph (1)(f), that
-- src:12503 | (i) the judge failed to comply with a statutory requirement for the making of the decision or order,
-- src:12504 | (ii) the decision or order was made in the absence of any evidence that a statutory requirement for the making of the decision or order was met, or
-- src:12505 | (iii) the decision or order was made as a result of reckless disregard for the truth, fraud, intentional misrepresentation of material facts or intentional omission to state material facts.
@ref s 573.1(3) (src:12482-12505)
DECLARE `s 573.1(3) the ground` IS ONE OF
    `s 573.1(3)(a)(i) failed to observe a principle of natural justice or failed or refused to exercise jurisdiction`
    `s 573.1(3)(a)(ii) the decision or order was made as a result of an irrelevant consideration or for an improper purpose`
    `s 573.1(3)(b)(i) failed to comply with a statutory requirement for the making of the decision or order`
    `s 573.1(3)(b)(ii) made in the absence of any evidence that a statutory requirement was met`
    `s 573.1(3)(b)(iii) made as a result of reckless disregard for the truth, fraud, intentional misrepresentation or intentional omission`
    `s 573.1(3)(b)(iv) the warrant is so vague or lacking in particularity that it authorizes an unreasonable search`
    `s 573.1(3)(b)(v) the warrant lacks a material term or condition that is required by law`
    `s 573.1(3)(c)(i) failed to follow a mandatory provision of this Act relating to the conduct of a preliminary inquiry`
    `s 573.1(3)(c)(ii) ordered the accused to stand trial when there was no evidence on which a properly instructed jury acting reasonably could convict`
    `s 573.1(3)(c)(iii) discharged the accused when there was some evidence on which a properly instructed jury acting reasonably could convict`
    `s 573.1(3)(d) erred in law`
    `s 573.1(3)(e)(i) the information or indictment failed to give the accused notice of the charge`
    `s 573.1(3)(e)(ii) the judge did not have jurisdiction to try the offence`
    `s 573.1(3)(e)(iii) the provision creating the offence is unconstitutional`
    `s 573.1(3)(f)(i) failed to comply with a statutory requirement for the making of the decision or order`
    `s 573.1(3)(f)(ii) made in the absence of any evidence that a statutory requirement was met`
    `s 573.1(3)(f)(iii) made as a result of reckless disregard for the truth, fraud, intentional misrepresentation or intentional omission`
    `s 573.1(3) none of those grounds`

-- The grounds that go with each kind of decision or order: (a) lists the grounds for every kind; (b) for paragraph (1)(a); (c) for (1)(b); (d) for (1)(c) or (d); (e) for (1)(e); (f) for (1)(f).
-- src:12482 | Grounds of review
-- src:12483 | (3) The judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may grant relief under subsection (4) only if the judge is satisfied that
-- src:12484 | (a) in the case of any decision or order mentioned in subsection (1),
-- src:12485 | (i) the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice failed to observe a principle of natural justice or failed or refused to exercise the judge’s jurisdiction, or
-- src:12486 | (ii) the decision or order was made as a result of an irrelevant consideration or for an improper purpose;
-- src:12487 | (b) in the case of a decision or order mentioned in paragraph (1)(a), that
-- src:12488 | (i) the judge failed to comply with a statutory requirement for the making of the decision or order,
-- src:12489 | (ii) the decision or order was made in the absence of any evidence that a statutory requirement for the making of the decision or order was met,
-- src:12490 | (iii) the decision or order was made as a result of reckless disregard for the truth, fraud, intentional misrepresentation of material facts or intentional omission to state material facts,
-- src:12491 | (iv) the warrant is so vague or lacking in particularity that it authorizes an unreasonable search, or
-- src:12492 | (v) the warrant lacks a material term or condition that is required by law;
-- src:12493 | (c) in the case of a decision or order mentioned in paragraph (1)(b), that the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice
-- src:12494 | (i) failed to follow a mandatory provision of this Act relating to the conduct of a preliminary inquiry,
-- src:12495 | (ii) ordered the accused to stand trial when there was no evidence adduced on which a properly instructed jury acting reasonably could convict, or
-- src:12496 | (iii) discharged the accused when there was some evidence adduced on which a properly instructed jury acting reasonably could convict;
-- src:12497 | (d) in the case of a decision or order mentioned in paragraph (1)(c) or (d), that the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice erred in law;
-- src:12498 | (e) in the case of a decision or order mentioned in paragraph (1)(e), that
-- src:12499 | (i) the information or indictment failed to give the accused notice of the charge,
-- src:12500 | (ii) the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice did not have jurisdiction to try the offence, or
-- src:12501 | (iii) the provision creating the offence alleged to have been committed by the accused is unconstitutional; or
-- src:12502 | (f) in the case of a decision or order mentioned in paragraph (1)(f), that
-- src:12503 | (i) the judge failed to comply with a statutory requirement for the making of the decision or order,
-- src:12504 | (ii) the decision or order was made in the absence of any evidence that a statutory requirement for the making of the decision or order was met, or
-- src:12505 | (iii) the decision or order was made as a result of reckless disregard for the truth, fraud, intentional misrepresentation of material facts or intentional omission to state material facts.
@ref s 573.1(3) (src:12482-12505)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 573.1(1) the kind of decision or order`
      ground IS A `s 573.1(3) the ground`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 573.1(3) the ground is one the subsection names for that kind of decision or order` MEANS
    CONSIDER ground
    WHEN `s 573.1(3)(a)(i) failed to observe a principle of natural justice or failed or refused to exercise jurisdiction` THEN NOT (kind EQUALS `s 573.1(1) some other kind of decision or order`)
    WHEN `s 573.1(3)(a)(ii) the decision or order was made as a result of an irrelevant consideration or for an improper purpose` THEN NOT (kind EQUALS `s 573.1(1) some other kind of decision or order`)
    WHEN `s 573.1(3)(b)(i) failed to comply with a statutory requirement for the making of the decision or order` THEN kind EQUALS `s 573.1(1)(a) relating to a warrant or summons`
    WHEN `s 573.1(3)(b)(ii) made in the absence of any evidence that a statutory requirement was met` THEN kind EQUALS `s 573.1(1)(a) relating to a warrant or summons`
    WHEN `s 573.1(3)(b)(iii) made as a result of reckless disregard for the truth, fraud, intentional misrepresentation or intentional omission` THEN kind EQUALS `s 573.1(1)(a) relating to a warrant or summons`
    WHEN `s 573.1(3)(b)(iv) the warrant is so vague or lacking in particularity that it authorizes an unreasonable search` THEN kind EQUALS `s 573.1(1)(a) relating to a warrant or summons`
    WHEN `s 573.1(3)(b)(v) the warrant lacks a material term or condition that is required by law` THEN kind EQUALS `s 573.1(1)(a) relating to a warrant or summons`
    WHEN `s 573.1(3)(c)(i) failed to follow a mandatory provision of this Act relating to the conduct of a preliminary inquiry` THEN kind EQUALS `s 573.1(1)(b) relating to the conduct of a preliminary inquiry, including an order under subsection 548(1)`
    WHEN `s 573.1(3)(c)(ii) ordered the accused to stand trial when there was no evidence on which a properly instructed jury acting reasonably could convict` THEN kind EQUALS `s 573.1(1)(b) relating to the conduct of a preliminary inquiry, including an order under subsection 548(1)`
    WHEN `s 573.1(3)(c)(iii) discharged the accused when there was some evidence on which a properly instructed jury acting reasonably could convict` THEN kind EQUALS `s 573.1(1)(b) relating to the conduct of a preliminary inquiry, including an order under subsection 548(1)`
    WHEN `s 573.1(3)(d) erred in law` THEN kind EQUALS `s 573.1(1)(c) relating to a subpoena` OR kind EQUALS `s 573.1(1)(d) relating to the publication or broadcasting of information or access to the court room`
    WHEN `s 573.1(3)(e)(i) the information or indictment failed to give the accused notice of the charge` THEN kind EQUALS `s 573.1(1)(e) to refuse to quash an information or indictment`
    WHEN `s 573.1(3)(e)(ii) the judge did not have jurisdiction to try the offence` THEN kind EQUALS `s 573.1(1)(e) to refuse to quash an information or indictment`
    WHEN `s 573.1(3)(e)(iii) the provision creating the offence is unconstitutional` THEN kind EQUALS `s 573.1(1)(e) to refuse to quash an information or indictment`
    WHEN `s 573.1(3)(f)(i) failed to comply with a statutory requirement for the making of the decision or order` THEN kind EQUALS `s 573.1(1)(f) relating to the detention, disposal or forfeiture of any thing seized under a warrant or order`
    WHEN `s 573.1(3)(f)(ii) made in the absence of any evidence that a statutory requirement was met` THEN kind EQUALS `s 573.1(1)(f) relating to the detention, disposal or forfeiture of any thing seized under a warrant or order`
    WHEN `s 573.1(3)(f)(iii) made as a result of reckless disregard for the truth, fraud, intentional misrepresentation or intentional omission` THEN kind EQUALS `s 573.1(1)(f) relating to the detention, disposal or forfeiture of any thing seized under a warrant or order`
    WHEN `s 573.1(3) none of those grounds` THEN FALSE

