-- src:12505 | (iii) the decision or order was made as a result of reckless disregard for the truth, fraud, intentional misrepresentation of material facts or intentional omission to state material facts.
@ref s 573.1(3) (src:12482-12505)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 573.1(1) the kind of decision or order`
      ground IS A `s 573.1(3) the ground`
      `the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut is satisfied that the ground is made out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573.1(3) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may grant relief under subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF `s 573.1(3) the ground is one the subsection names for that kind of decision or order` kind ground AND `the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut is satisfied that the ground is made out`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may grant relief under subsection (4) only if the judge is satisfied that" [M-a]

-- (4): on the hearing, the judge may do one or more of (a) to (g). (f) refuse relief if the judge is of the opinion that no substantial wrong or miscarriage of justice has occurred or that the subject-matter should be determined at trial or on appeal.
-- src:12506 | Powers of judge
-- src:12507 | (4) On the hearing of the application for review, the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may do one or more of the following:
-- src:12508 | (a) order a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice to do any act or thing that the judge or any other judge of that court failed or refused to do or has delayed in doing;
-- src:12509 | (b) prohibit or restrain a decision, order or proceeding of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice;
-- src:12510 | (c) declare invalid or unlawful, quash or set aside, in whole or in part, a decision, order or proceeding of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice;
-- src:12511 | (d) refer back for determination in accordance with any directions that the judge considers to be appropriate, a decision, order or proceeding of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice;
-- src:12512 | (e) grant any remedy under subsection 24(1) of the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms;
-- src:12513 | (f) refuse to grant any relief if the judge is of the opinion that no substantial wrong or miscarriage of justice has occurred or that the subject-matter of the application should be determined at trial or on appeal; and
-- src:12514 | (g) dismiss the application.
@ref s 573.1(4) (src:12506-12514)
DECLARE `s 573.1(4) what the judge does` IS ONE OF
    `s 573.1(4)(a) order a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice to do any act or thing that the judge or any other judge of that court failed or refused to do or has delayed in doing`
    `s 573.1(4)(b) prohibit or restrain a decision, order or proceeding of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice`
    `s 573.1(4)(c) declare invalid or unlawful, quash or set aside, in whole or in part, a decision, order or proceeding`
    `s 573.1(4)(d) refer back for determination in accordance with any directions the judge considers appropriate`
    `s 573.1(4)(e) grant any remedy under subsection 24(1) of the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms`
    `s 573.1(4)(f) refuse to grant any relief`
    `s 573.1(4)(g) dismiss the application`
    `s 573.1(4) some other order`

-- src:12506 | Powers of judge
-- src:12507 | (4) On the hearing of the application for review, the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may do one or more of the following:
-- src:12508 | (a) order a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice to do any act or thing that the judge or any other judge of that court failed or refused to do or has delayed in doing;
-- src:12509 | (b) prohibit or restrain a decision, order or proceeding of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice;
-- src:12510 | (c) declare invalid or unlawful, quash or set aside, in whole or in part, a decision, order or proceeding of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice;
-- src:12511 | (d) refer back for determination in accordance with any directions that the judge considers to be appropriate, a decision, order or proceeding of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice;
-- src:12512 | (e) grant any remedy under subsection 24(1) of the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms;
-- src:12513 | (f) refuse to grant any relief if the judge is of the opinion that no substantial wrong or miscarriage of justice has occurred or that the subject-matter of the application should be determined at trial or on appeal; and
-- src:12514 | (g) dismiss the application.
@ref s 573.1(4) (src:12506-12514)
GIVEN `the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut is hearing an application for review` IS A BOOLEAN
      step IS A `s 573.1(4) what the judge does`
      `the judge is of the opinion that no substantial wrong or miscarriage of justice has occurred or that the subject-matter of the application should be determined at trial or on appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573.1(4) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may do this on the hearing of the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut is hearing an application for review` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On the hearing of the application for review"
        IF step EQUALS `s 573.1(4) some other order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may do one or more of the following"
        IF step EQUALS `s 573.1(4)(f) refuse to grant any relief` AND (NOT `the judge is of the opinion that no substantial wrong or miscarriage of justice has occurred or that the subject-matter of the application should be determined at trial or on appeal`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "refuse to grant any relief if the judge is of the opinion that no substantial wrong or miscarriage of justice has occurred" [F:may-if]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12515 | Interim orders
-- src:12516 | (5) If an application for review is made, a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may make any interim order that the judge considers appropriate pending the final disposition of the application for review.
@ref s 573.1(5) (src:12515-12516)
GIVEN `an application for review is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573.1(5) a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may make an interim order pending the final disposition` MEANS
    IF `an application for review is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an application for review is made, a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may make any interim order" [F:may-if]

-- (6): the person who proposes to apply shall do so in the manner and within the period directed by rules of court (the rules are outside the sources: the facts are inputs), except that a judge may at any time extend any period specified in the rules.
-- src:12517 | Rules
-- src:12518 | (6) A person who proposes to make an application for review shall do so in the manner and within the period that may be directed by rules of court, except that a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may at any time extend any period specified in the rules.
@ref s 573.1(6) (src:12517-12518)
GIVEN `the application is made in the manner directed by rules of court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made within the period specified in the rules of court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut has extended the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573.1(6) the application is made as the rules of court direct` MEANS
    IF `the application is made in the manner directed by rules of court` AND (`the application is made within the period specified in the rules of court` OR `a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut has extended the period`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall do so in the manner and within the period that may be directed by rules of court, except that a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may at any time extend any period" [M-a] [F:duty]

-- src:12517 | Rules
-- src:12518 | (6) A person who proposes to make an application for review shall do so in the manner and within the period that may be directed by rules of court, except that a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may at any time extend any period specified in the rules.
@ref s 573.1(6) (src:12517-12518)
GIVEN `the period is one specified in the rules of court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573.1(6) a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may extend the period at any time` MEANS
    IF `the period is one specified in the rules of court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may at any time extend any period specified in the rules" [F:may-if]

-- src:12519 | Appeal
-- src:12520 | (7) An appeal lies to the Court of Appeal of Nunavut against a decision or order made under subsection (4). The provisions of Part XXI apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the appeal.
@ref s 573.1(7) (src:12519-12520)
GIVEN `the decision or order was made under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573.1(7) an appeal lies to the Court of Appeal of Nunavut and the provisions of Part XXI apply to it` MEANS
    IF `the decision or order was made under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against a decision or order made under subsection (4)"

§ `Section 573.2 -- Habeas corpus`

-- (1): habeas corpus proceedings may be brought before a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut in respect of an order made or warrant issued by a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice, except where (a) or (b).
-- src:12522 | 573.2 (1) Habeas corpus proceedings may be brought before a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut in respect of an order made or warrant issued by a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice, except where
-- src:12523 | (a) the order or warrant is of a kind that could only be made or issued in a province or a territory other than Nunavut by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552; or
-- src:12524 | (b) another statutory right of review or appeal is available.
@ref s 573.2(1) (src:12522-12524)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in respect of an order made or warrant issued by a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order or warrant is of a kind that could only be made or issued in a province or a territory other than Nunavut by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another statutory right of review or appeal is available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573.2(1) habeas corpus proceedings may be brought before a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are in respect of an order made or warrant issued by a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of an order made or warrant issued by a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice"
        IF `the order or warrant is of a kind that could only be made or issued in a province or a territory other than Nunavut by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552` OR `another statutory right of review or appeal is available` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except where (a) the order or warrant is of a kind that could only be made or issued in a province or a territory other than Nunavut" [F:unless] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12525 | Exception
-- src:12526 | (2) Despite subsection (1), habeas corpus proceedings may be brought before a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut with respect to an order or warrant of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice if the proceedings are brought to challenge the constitutionality of a person’s detention or confinement.
@ref s 573.2(2) (src:12525-12526)
GIVEN `the proceedings are with respect to an order or warrant of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are brought to challenge the constitutionality of a person’s detention or confinement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573.2(2) habeas corpus proceedings may be brought despite subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are with respect to an order or warrant of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice` AND `the proceedings are brought to challenge the constitutionality of a person’s detention or confinement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the proceedings are brought to challenge the constitutionality of a person’s detention or confinement" [F:may-if]

-- src:12522 | 573.2 (1) Habeas corpus proceedings may be brought before a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut in respect of an order made or warrant issued by a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice, except where
-- src:12523 | (a) the order or warrant is of a kind that could only be made or issued in a province or a territory other than Nunavut by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552; or
-- src:12524 | (b) another statutory right of review or appeal is available.
-- src:12525 | Exception
-- src:12526 | (2) Despite subsection (1), habeas corpus proceedings may be brought before a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut with respect to an order or warrant of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice if the proceedings are brought to challenge the constitutionality of a person’s detention or confinement.
@ref s 573.2(1) and (2) (src:12522-12526)
GIVEN `the answer of s 573.2(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 573.2(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573.2 habeas corpus proceedings may be brought, taking subsections (1) and (2) together` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 573.2(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE `the answer of s 573.2(1)`

-- src:12527 | Provisions apply
-- src:12528 | (3) Subsections 784(2) to (6) apply in respect of any proceedings brought under subsection (1) or (2).
@ref s 573.2(3) (src:12527-12528)
GIVEN `the proceedings are brought under subsection 573.2(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573.2(3) subsections 784(2) to (6) apply to the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are brought under subsection 573.2(1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of any proceedings brought under subsection (1) or (2)"
